1
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:14,210
Excuse me, officer.

2
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:15,270
Can you help me?

3
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:16,510
Sure.

4
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:17,430
Can you tell me

5
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:21,720
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

6
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,180
Riverdale, New York."

7
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,310
You should take the number 1 subway.

8
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,400
Is there a station near here?

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,320
Yes. The station's that way.

10
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,700
You should take the number 1 train

11
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:30,950
to Van Cortlandt Park.

12
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:34,110
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

13
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:35,230
Anytime. Good luck.

14
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:38,690
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

15
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:40,910
Thank you.

16
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:57,220
You're welcome.

17
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:59,800
Is this pink too bright for me?

18
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:09,890
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

19
00:01:09,890 --> 00:01:14,550
Try this. It's size eight.

20
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:16,460
But I wear size ten.

21
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:21,120
How about green? It's size ten.

22
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,840
Let me try it on.

23
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:29,630
I'm taking too much of your time.

24
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:30,830
It's six o'clock.

25
00:01:30,830 --> 00:01:32,610
Where's my husband?

26
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,780
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

27
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:37,060
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

28
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:41,580
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

29
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:42,970
I'll take this green sweater.

30
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,310
I like the color on me, don't you?

31
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:52,100
I think it looks terrific on you.

32
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,310
I'm sorry I'm so late.

33
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:56,220
I had a really bad day.

34
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,350
It's ten after six. We're late.

35
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:00,460
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

36
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:03,540
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

37
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,860
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

38
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:07,890
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

39
00:02:07,890 --> 00:02:10,310
I lost a whole day's work.

40
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:13,070
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

41
00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:21,260
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

42
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:22,320
Hello.

43
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,910
Yes. The number, please,

44
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:29,230
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

45
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:35,280
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

46
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:38,000
Thank you.

47
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,260
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

48
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,440
Hello.

49
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:45,310
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

50
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:48,790
a small canvas bag,

51
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:55,560
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

52
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,730
Maybe someone will find it.

53
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:01,010
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

54
00:03:01,010 --> 00:03:04,430
And the telephone number is five five five...

55
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:10,840
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

56
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:13,920
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

57
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,400
Thanks, anyway.

58
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,020
There was a girl on the ferry.

59
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:21,140
Now maybe...

60
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:24,140
Tell me about it on the way home.
